-- Source module: Solutions.KIL5Edge
/-!
# KIL5: the uniform frame change (template lists, child calls through the descriptor)

The frame change `Φ_X` of a level is the run of a template list `Ts` (KIL5Tpl):

* a shift template `T` is the fixed program `stepU m rXs T` (KIL4StepH), reading the modulus
  `N` and the volumes from the level registers;
* an interchange template `sw a b` is `swC m j0 a b`: push the child descriptor (level `k - 1`,
  `L / W`, `vol A · N^a`, `N^(m-1-a) · vol B · N^(b-m)`, `N^(m+m-1-b) · vol Cs`) computed from
  the level registers, call the uniform procedure `j0`, pop the descriptor.

Both codes depend only on `m`, `j0` and the template, not on the level, the modulus or the
sizes.  `edgeCU_runs`: the code of `Ts` computes `runC` of the denoted steps (any child function
whose call code is correct); `swC_runs`: the call wrapper realises a child given by a recursive
specification of the procedure `j0` on descriptor states.
-/

